    "markdown": "# Knowledge Base: cantor-diagonalization-oq-03-oq-01-oq-03\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nThe problem is to formalize Godel's first incompleteness theorem as an instance of the Lawvere Fixed-Point Theorem. The intended interpretation is: values are sentences, point-surjectivity is supplied by the diagonal lemma, and the self-map is negated provability, yielding a true but unprovable sentence.\n\n---\n\n## Local Evidence\n\nThe parent proof cantor-diagonalization-oq-03-oq-01 provides the Lawvere FPT gallery result. The problem note records that a Lean 4 derivation of the Godel instance and a Lean 4 diagonal lemma for provability logic remain open.\n\n---\n\n## Technical Risks\n\nThe local notes flag formal-system encoding, Godel numbering or equivalent syntax machinery, provability logic, and the diagonal lemma as the hard prerequisites. Mathlib support for these pieces still needs a focused search.\n\n---\n\n## Dead Ends\n\nNo dead ends are recorded in the local research state.\n"
